  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Which of the following is a permutation?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Choose 2 of 4 students to form a group, without regard to order",
    "B": "Put 4 books into a pile, without distinguishing left from right",
    "C": "Choose 2 of 4 students and arrange them in order",
    "D": "Consider only which people were selected"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A permutation involves arranging items in order. Forming a group without regard to order is a combination.\n\nC explicitly requires an ordered selection, whereas A and D disregard order. If B means an unordered pile, the unique answer is C. If B means a vertical stack of distinct books whose top-to-bottom order is distinguished, swapping the top two books changes the arrangement, so B is also a permutation. Ignoring left and right does not rule out vertical order. Thus C is the intended answer under the unordered-pile interpretation of B; under the ordered-stack interpretation, both B and C qualify.",
